=== OBSERVATIONS (backlog, NOT failures) ===

  O1. Chart "Cumulative balance" series vs the KPI combined figure.
      On the fixture the series ends at -1129.03 while the Budget/verdict
      combined delta is +1180.70 (balance is sign-inverted, so -1180.70 is
      expected). The 51.67 gap is a MONTHS-BASIS difference that is
      PRE-EXISTING on master: `git show master:internal/handlers/dashboard/
      handlers.go` shows the loop accrued a flat `combinedTarget` per
      CALENDAR month, while metrics.Calculate uses day-fraction
      MonthsBetween. HC1 correctly clipped the healthcare share
      (handlers.go:694) but left the living share flat, exactly as master
      had it. Arithmetic: chart living 6x1000 = 6000 vs metrics 5946.61
      (+53.39); chart healthcare 1871.00 vs metrics 1872.69 (-1.69); net
      51.70. Criterion 4 names the "budget-vs-actual target LINE", which
      does agree exactly (1314.9171270718232). Not an HC1 regression.

  O2. The oracle's header comment arithmetic is slightly off (it states
      monthsInRange 5.94682 / living +1,253.18 / combined +1,130.49 / chart
      1,314.90; the true rendered figures are 5.946612 / +1,253.39 /
      +1,180.70 / 1314.9171). The oracle's actual ASSERTIONS are regex- and
      sign-based, so they are unaffected; only the explanatory comment is
      imprecise.

  O3. metrics.Comparison calls HealthcareCoverageStart(data) on its raw
      `data` param rather than data.Active(). Harmless today because both
      production callers (handlers.go:110, 190) already pass data.Active(),
      but the derivation would silently pick up suppressed duplicates if a
      future caller passed a raw set. Related to gap 3b.

  O4. Spec's declared out-of-scope items confirmed not evaluated here: the
      live MCP-vs-dashboard combined-delta disagreement and the live-binary
      rebuild figure shift. All my figures are fixture-based.
